{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2266 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "cdd39d1fae7eba887d2e9c1163f8cf65eefbd45ade153eb94eb60e1c7148adaf" :edb/db-before-t 2265 :edb/db-after-t 2266 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535578 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:52:37.261Z" 13194139535578 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355891 13194139535578 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355898 13194139535578 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355919 13194139535578 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355905 13194139535578 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355912 13194139535578 true] [17592186355891 1017 #edb/ref 17592186355892 13194139535578 true] [17592186355891 1089 "q-108735" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355891 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535578 true] [17592186355891 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3x+6y.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+2y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355891 1113 #uuid "f3db89b1-1677-58e1-bc7f-a28efef6c8ab" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355891 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3(x+2y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1) & =3z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=6z+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=6z+1.$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355892 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355893 13194139535