function $f(z)?$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355898 1113 #uuid "6cab1a85-35c1-5dc8-a717-af6a11e616be" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355898 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(x+4y)-1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+4y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1) & =\\frac{2z-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2z.$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355900 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355901 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355902 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355903 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355904 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1041 "selection" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355900 13194139535578 true] [17592186355899 1110 #uuid "922b6933-dba3-587c-9670-45e3901e8f12" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355900 1034 "2z" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355900 1111 #uuid "51612dac-eda1-5ccc-b7d8-6cd0310d07fb" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355901 1034 "3-2z" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355901 1111 #uuid "d81f953d-07ad-56aa-8ae3-a57b427fb1f4" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355902 1034 "\\frac{z+2}{2}" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355902 1111 #uuid "4eada411-719d-5529-a53c-a219eb07561f" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355903 1034 "6-z" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355903 1111 #uuid "87f7fedc-9cb3-53ef-b585-0159f878b516" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355904 1034 "\\frac{2z-1}{4}" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355904 1111 #uuid "37af3e1d-35f4-5288-9d03-489f08189fcb" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355905 1017 #edb/ref 17592186355906 13194139535578 true] [17592186355905 1089 "q-108780" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355905 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535578 true] [17592186355905 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+3y)-1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(g(x,y))=-6x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355905 1113 #uuid "7a64bfa3-c0ef-53da-9e38-b194f0c2decf" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355905 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2{sin}^{2}⁡(3(x+y))-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =2{sin}^{2}⁡(3z)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2{sin}^{2}⁡(3z).\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡(3z)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}⁡(3z)\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3z) & =2x+K \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡(3z) & =-6x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-3K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+3y)=-6x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\ng(x,y)=3x+3y.\n$$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355907 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355908 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355909 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355910 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355911 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1041 "selection" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355907 13194139535578 true] [17592186355906 1110 #uuid "9fe21f47-1ebc-507f-aacc-b133d33bf32a" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355907 1034 "3x+3y" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355907 1111 #uuid "c20c8d35-033b-5ff5-86e7-e038af428d6b" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355908 1034 "3x+3y-1" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355908 1111 #uuid "97e8845f-8758-5144-9527-a7c31c2b94e7" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355909 1034 "x+y" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355909 1111 #uuid "73380151-d5fd-583b-bb58-46a0787ca09e" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355910 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355910 1111 #uuid "91ec4203-e15e-5428-9db4-993948a8fda2" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355911 1034 "3-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355911 1111 #uuid "be66a95b-c1c9-57ac-925a-f56a550b3b13" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355912 1017 #edb/ref 17592186355913 13194139535578 true] [17592186355912 1089 "q-108849" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355912 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535578 true] [17592186355912 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x-2y).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=6x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355912 1113 #uuid "0b284936-a6fa-5551-8450-4970d6b1619b" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355912 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2(x-y))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x-y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2z).\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2z)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2z)\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2z) & =3x+K \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2z) & =6x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y)=6x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y).\n$$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355914 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355915 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355916 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355917 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355918 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1041 "selection" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355915 13194139535578 true] [17592186355913 1110 #uuid "eead8314-3740-5c28-bddb-cc252bc74799" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355914 1034 "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x-2y)" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355914 1111 #uuid "13f461a0-2479-552e-b87d-58e400a3eb5a" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355915 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-2y)" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355915 1111 #uuid "7b44eaa0-97f9-5b5e-961e-28ced49419d2" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355916 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-2y)" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355916 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355916 1111 #uuid "cc58c8ab-1c38-5678-be04-b460d02f196a" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355917 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-2y)" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355917 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355917 1111 #uuid "43beb5a9-92aa-566d-a573-b1a395ab936f" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355918 1034 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x-2y)" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355918 1111 #uuid "ee6b4f30-d9c6-5511-960e-6bb6d54f7e76" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355919 1017 #edb/ref 17592186355920 13194139535578 true] [17592186355919 1089 "q-149744" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355919 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535578 true] [17592186355919 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{10x+2y}{5x+y+1}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=5x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355919 1113 #uuid "fd506b7c-591c-5881-937e-94db4a95aca3" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355919 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(5x+y)}{(5x+y)+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=5x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-5 & =\\frac{2z}{z+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{7z+5}{z+1}.$" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355921 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355922 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355923 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355924 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355925 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1041 "selection" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355925 13194139535578 true] [17592186355920 1110 #uuid "933c1c0d-edf0-5bb3-bb4b-33cda388d169" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355921 1034 "\\frac{1-5z}{z+1}" 13194139535578 true] [17592186355921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535578 true] [17592186355921 1111 #uuid "9a03db04-63f8-50bf-8a45-c8130f553bc0" 13194139535578 true] [1759